{
  "id": "28250_kerikomu",
  "headword": "{蹴|け}り{込|こ}む",
  "reading": "けりこむ",
  "romaji": "kerikomu",
  "part_of_speech": "verb (godan)",
  "gloss": "to kick (the ball) into; to kick in",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to kick into; to kick (a ball) in",
      "explanation": "To send something into a target or enclosed space by kicking. Most often used in sports of kicking a ball into the goal. The destination is marked with に."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "28250_kerikomu_ex1",
      "japanese": "ボールをゴールに{蹴|け}り{込|こ}む。",
      "english": "To kick the ball into the goal.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "28250_kerikomu_ex2",
      "japanese": "{鋭|するど}いシュートをゴールに{蹴|け}り{込|こ}んだ。",
      "english": "He kicked a sharp shot into the goal.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "28250_kerikomu_ex3",
      "japanese": "{試合終了間際|しあいしゅうりょうまぎわ}に{逆転|ぎゃくてん}ゴールを{蹴|け}り{込|こ}んで{勝利|しょうり}した。",
      "english": "He kicked in the go-ahead goal just before the final whistle and won the match.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Compound of {蹴|け}る (to kick) + {込|こ}む (to put/send into). The {込|こ}む suffix adds the sense of sending something into a space or target.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Transitive ({他動詞|たどうし}).\n- Pattern: Xを{場所|ばしょ}に{蹴|け}り{込|こ}む\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- ゴールに{蹴|け}り{込|こ}む: kick into the goal\n- ネットに{蹴|け}り{込|こ}む: kick into the net\n- {決勝点|けっしょうてん}を{蹴|け}り{込|こ}む: kick in the winning goal",
